<title>SOUTH AFRICA: TABLE -S.Africa Apr-Jun spending 14.4 pct up.</title>
<headline>TABLE -S.Africa Apr-Jun spending 14.4 pct up.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's Finance Department said on Thursday that 14.65 billion rand was requested from the exchequer in June by government departments and agencies, compared to May's 14.46 billion rand.</p>
<p>This brought exchequer issues for the first three months of the financial year (April to June) to 46.625 billion rand, the department said in a statement. The total was 14.4 percent up on the 40.752 billion rand issued over the same period a year ago.</p>
<p>Detailed breakdown:</p>
<p>(rand bln)		Jun '97  Jun '96  Apr/Jun '97  Apr/Jun '96</p>
<p>Exchequer issues	14.65    11.19    46.62	  40.75</p>
<p>Total revenue	   11.83     9.80    33.77	  29.89</p>
<p>Borrowing requirement  1.79     1.93    12.16	  15.22</p>
<p>Total financing	  8.14     1.68    18.50	  14.97</p>
<p>Main sources of revenue:</p>
<p>			    May '97  May '96  Apr/May '97  Apr/May '96</p>
<p>Income tax		5.10     4.51     11.06	  10.37</p>
<p>Sales tax/VAT	   3.16     2.72	5.48	   5.11</p>
<p>Customs and Excise    1.77     1.60	2.93	   2.84</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27 11 482-1003</p>
</text>
